# PR quality gates

Never merge into `main` unless every gate below is green. Failures are blocking: fix, commit, re-run. Do not merge a red, skipped, or unverified PR.

## Required gates

From the repo root, after the last change and before merge:

```
pnpm test
pnpm exec prettier --check .
pnpm lint
pnpm typecheck
pnpm build
```

All must exit 0.

- **Unit tests** (`pnpm test`): every package/app suite passes. Do not skip tests, delete assertions to go green, or use `--no-verify`.
- **Formatting** (`pnpm exec prettier --check .` and `pnpm lint`): no prettier drift and no eslint failures. Apply `pnpm exec prettier --write .`, then lint, then commit.
- **Types** (`pnpm typecheck`): clean typecheck.
- **Build** (`pnpm build`): production build succeeds.

If GitHub checks cover any of these (or **Supabase Preview** when `supabase/**` changed), wait until they pass. Local green does not excuse a failing required CI check.

```
# ❌ BAD — merge while a gate is red or unrun
gh pr merge

# ✅ GOOD — every command exits 0 and required CI is green, then merge
pnpm test && pnpm exec prettier --check . && pnpm lint && pnpm typecheck && pnpm build
```
